work_experience.description:
Belonging to Product Development Team (Development of CNC High Speed Machining Centers and Gantries), my daily tasks consist of: 

> Designing the manufacturing process of New Products during the Product Development Phase; 
> Structuring and setting up of the product in the relevant (IT) platform/system (Definition of the MBOM); 
> Design For Manufacturing: defining Product Modification / Sub-Groups Specifications in order to meet targeted Cost and Lead Time; 
> Managing schedule of Prototype Development. Assure the information flow between Industrial Operations and the Product Development; 
> Defining/Implementing/Measuring the KPIs of Product Development: Stock Reduction, Product Family Costs, Product (Project) Delivery Time; 

In parallel, my role inside the internal "Industrialization Project" consists of: 

> Coordination of cross-functional (Production & Logistics - Purchasing - Product Development) initiatives to reduce: Product Cost, Product Lead Time, Standard Production Process Costs; 
> Lead bi-weekly Report to the Directive Board of the Status of the project through the use of the above-mentioned KPIs; 
> Lead the study for the change of the manufacturing strategy of Castres Plant: from Make to Order to Finish to Order. Coordinate relative activities of a multi-disciplinary team (Planning, Manufacturing, Logistics, Product Development, Purchasing);

As a part of a big Multi-Country project with a Key Customer, my main responsibilities as a Site Engineer were: 

> Troubleshooting and on-Site technical assistance; 
> Designing, planning and implementing tests, retrofits and engineering activities in house and at the customer’s site. (Buffalo Area, NY, US); 
> Definition of the Non-Conformity Costs and Long-Term Countermeasures definition through Standard Product modifications; 
> Manage customer relationship from site. Ensure the information flow between the HQ and the Customer's Site; 
> Propose/Implement solutions to increase productivity and availability of the manufacturing line;

As a research fellow, my main responsibilities were: 

> Finding the relevant academic literature for the research topic (development of a grip model for pneumatic tires under wet conditions, in collaboration with Bridgestone Europe); 
> Development of the model in Matlab Environment; 
> Determination of empirical coefficients through experimental tests; 
> Validation of the model via comparison of numerical and experimental data; 

The Internship was aimed at writing the MSc thesis, whose title was: “A physical model for the study of the effect of roughness and rubber properties on the behavior of pneumatic tires”
